    "Inspected opening witnesses: Brill PDF 83–84 and Dar Ibn Kathir PDF 82–84. The modern print inserts an additional opening heading, while the historical and selected digital source do not. The prototype preserves the selected source’s chapter grouping.",
    "The selected combined report 295 corresponds to modern printed 299–301; the two English bodies and historical print retain the combined wording. Reference identities are matched individually, not inferred as a constant offset.",
    "Full chains and reporting verbs are retained from the selected Arabic. Historical variants in 291, 292, 294 and 296 are disclosed; all eight admitted Arabic paragraphs remain unchanged.",
    "All other numbered records remain unreviewed intake. No human certification or production publication is implied.",
    "At 292 the embedded Aisha attribution remains an independent chain segment in its source position. A feminine informed-me verb now participates in the reporting-verb validator.",
    "At 294 the two clothing words are distinguished, with the lexical reference pointing to the inspected commentary page 343. At 296 the timing phrase remains provisional and carries a separate visible uncertainty note.",
    "Closing Khalid/Jarir and Sufyan corroborations remain in 296 and 297. Book and two chapter introductions remain Arabic, separately browsable with English pending."
